  "public": true,
  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:auditability",
  "domain": "governance",
  "definition": "Auditability is the property of a system, process, or record that allows an independent party to examine and verify its actions, decisions, and state against expected behaviour or policy. It depends on complete, tamper-evident records \u2014 logs, audit trails, and provenance \u2014 that establish who did what, when, and why, enabling accountability and compliance review. Auditability is a foundational governance requirement for trustworthy financial, blockchain, and AI systems.",
